  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that the compound (2s,3r,4r)-3-Hydroxy-4-methyl-2-(eicos-11'-yn-19'-enyl)butanolide exerts its biological effects on prostate cells through a series of target interactions. This compound is identified as a target of SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and Bungeiside A. All of these compounds are ultimately linked to prostate cells as their targets. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, indicating that the compound may act through a shared mechanism involving the modulation of prostate cell activity. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that the compound interacts with prostate cells via a target-mediated pathway, possibly through the activation of specific signaling pathways or the direct influence on cellular processes. The evidence does not provide a clear distinction between the specific mechanisms involved, but it highlights a strong association between the compound and prostate cell targets, suggesting a potential role in prostate-related biological processes.",
